It is a cold Saturday morning.
I am at a large outdoor market in the city.
There are many busy people here.
I am a little cold, so I walk over to a coffee cart.
I would like to buy a black coffee to keep warm.
The man in the cart smiles at me.
"How much is a cup of coffee?" I ask.
"It costs twenty-five kroner," he answers.
I search for coins in my pocket.
I find exactly twenty-five kroner and give him the money.
He hands me the coffee.
The cup is lovely and warm in my hands.
I drink a little and walk further among the many stalls.
